[i]The morning dew fills your lungs with fresh air
[i]Mornings are usually noisy with the three bickering over small things
[i]Today was different
[i]It was weirdly quiet
[i]For they were all busy with their own activities
- Talk to Marius
	[i]You see Sir Marius busy with the map
	[i]You decide not to disturb him
	- Talk to Lea
		[i]You see Dame Mikhelea mindlessly stir a pot filled with porridge
		join Ardana (d) left
		Ardana: Dame Mikhelea?
		join Mikhelea (d) right
		Mikhelea: Your highness!
		Mikhelea (d): You're awake!
		Mikhelea: Would you care to pass me the bowl?
		[i]You pass the bowl to Dame Mikhelea
		[i]You can't help but notice the slight sweat on the palm of her hand
		[i]Before she could take it from your hands, you pull back
		Ardana: Hot is it?
		Mikhelea (shock): ...
		Mikhelea (nervous): Like the desert in summer…
		leave Mikhelea
		Ardana (suspicious): Really?
		Ardana: The wind seems to disagree.
		Ardana: Is there something you’re hiding from me-
		[i]A voice disturbs your conversation with Dame Mikhelea
		Random: Now your highness, let’s not disturb Dame Lea.
		join Alfonso right
		[i]Sir Alfonso looks down at you with a solemn look
		[i]He takes the bowl from your hand and gives it to Dame Mikhelea
		[i]You feel the tension shift as the cold air springs up your spine
		[i]You’ve never seen the calm Sir Alfonso take something so seriously
		[i]You decide to busy yourself with something else
		leave --All--
	- Talk to Alfonso
		[i]You see Sir Alfonso tidy up the cluttered items around your camp
		[i]You couldn’t see his facial expression
		[i]But you could tell he was dazed and bothered
		[i]You decide to help him tidy
		join Ardana (d) left
		join Alfonso (shocked) right
		Ardana: Would you like help, Sir Alfonso?
		Alfonso (shocked): ...
		Alfonso (nervous): Why thank you for the offer.
		Alfonso: ...
		[i]Sir Alfonso looks around the camp hesitantly
		Alfonso: there, uhm.
		Alfonso: Why don’t your highness help Dame Lea with the porridge?
		[i]Confused, Dame Mikhelea didn’t look like she was struggling serving the porridge
		[i]Despite that, you start walking towards her
		[i]The wind catches your hair, leaving behind you in disarray
		[i]With it a letter drifts pass you
		[i]It catches your eye as you reach to grab it
		[i]You managed to read the recipient line
		“To her highness, Princess-”
		Alfonso: WOah!
		Alfonso: So sorry, your highness.
		Alfonso: These are my personal belongings.
		Alfonso: It seemed to slip past my fingers.
		Alfonso: ...
		Ardana (suspicious): Are you sure?
		Ardana: It seemed it was addressed to me.
		Alfonso: No, no. I'm very sure.
		Ardana: You aren’t lying…
		Ardana: Are you?
		Alfonso: I...
		Alfonso (smile): would [b]never.
		Alfonso: ...
		leave --All--
